ic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-01T00:21:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T11:13:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproduceable in: 4.6.stable - 4.5.stable (those were the only versions I tested, I am not certain if it exists in previous versions)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) UHD Graphics (Intel Corporation; 26.20.100.7926) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-1035G1 CPU @ 1.00GHz (8 threads) - 11.78 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen migrating my project from Godot 4.5 to 4.6 I experienced some crashes, forcing the project to open in Recovery Mode. While opening in Recovery Mode, I resized the editor and applied the changes, restarting the editor. When the editor had restarted, it was no longer in Recovery Mode. I think the mode should persist even after performing a restart to apply changes.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open in Recovery Mode\n2. Edit an editor setting that requires a restart\n3. Restart the editor\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115694/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}